\ A const the startup file defines belongs to the base scope, as the prelude's consts do. `check`
\ accepts a redefinition of it, because its definitions never run. The analysis context starts
\ with no frame of its own below this file's, so the guard cannot see the startup file's const.

startup-const: ( -- x ) [ 2 ] ;
use-startup-const: ( -- x ) [ startup-const ] ;
